From 8dc537d8c003ac576736c02eac285df1d5189f0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:32:42 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 18e: route HTML tab fullscreen to the host

Implement the browser-less WebContentsDelegate fullscreen contract: a presented tab with a registered host callback enters Chromium tab fullscreen, the host receives an entered event to make its window fullscreen, and the renderer is resynchronized so the page's request resolves. Escape, page exit, navigation, hiding, close, host exit and callback replacement leave fullscreen with a typed exit reason. Without a callback page requests are refused, as before. ABI 1.27 / bridge 0.29.0; build p73, native refusal, entry and host/escape/page/hidden/close exits pass.

Last rebased: 2026-11-04 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
